# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sample documents — NOT COMMITTED BY DEFAULT
#
# The files at the repo root are real internal enterprise documents. At least
# one (FROGSLEAP_BUSINESS LICENSE.pdf) contains personal data: national ID
# numbers, dates of birth, and home addresses of named individuals. Others
# contain commercial pricing.
#
# They are therefore excluded from git so that pushing this repository —
# especially to a public remote — cannot disclose them. The pipeline reads
# them in place from the repo root; nothing depends on them being tracked.
#
# `samples/MANIFEST.json` IS committed: it records each file's name, size,
# SHA-256 and detected type, so the corpus is documented and verifiable
# without distributing its contents.
#
# If this repository is private and its policy permits committing these
# documents, delete this block and run `git add` explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.pdf
/*.docx
/*.xlsx
/*.pptx
/*.doc
/*.xls
/*.ppt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.so

# Project caches / model weights (redirected off the OS drive, never committed)
.cache/
*.pth
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Run artifacts — regenerated by `run` / `compare` / `inspect` / failure report
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

# Local experiment artifacts. The question, config and conclusions ARE
# committed (README.md / config.yaml / results.json / observations.md);
# bulky per-run output is not.
experiments/**/outputs/
experiments/**/rendered/
experiments/**/*.png
experiments/**/*.jpg

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Test / lint
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log
